Sval: a link from another app that is a download leaves no peek or tab

A link from another app opens in a peek, or in a tab Sval opens for it, and
when Gecko hands its first load to the external helper app service that
window or tab is left empty: Gecko closes one only when it has an opener to
fall back to (MaybeCloseWindowHelper), which such a link never has. The
download's start is where Sval learns of it with the browsing context it
came from (SvalLinkDownloads.handOver), and the announcement waits for the
peek to close and an ordinary window to be in front, since the panel opens
only in the active window. No chrome API reaches this: the announcement is
made inside DownloadsDataCtor, as the download's first change arrives, with
no hook before it.

diff --git a/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs b/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
index 1584b53142..0290cf68a4 100644
--- a/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/downloads/DownloadsCommon.sys.mjs
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@ const lazy = {};
 ChromeUtils.defineESModuleGetters(lazy, {
   SvalDownloadWorkspaces:
     "moz-src:///browser/components/sval/SvalDownloadWorkspaces.sys.mjs",
+  SvalLinkDownloads:
+    "moz-src:///browser/components/sval/SvalLinkDownloads.sys.mjs",
   BrowserWindowTracker: "resource:///modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs",
   DownloadHistory: "resource://gre/modules/DownloadHistory.sys.mjs",
   DownloadUtils: "resource://gre/modules/DownloadUtils.sys.mjs",
@@ -930,11 +932,20 @@ DownloadsDataCtor.prototype = {
 
     if (!download.newDownloadNotified) {
       download.newDownloadNotified = true;
-      this._notifyDownloadEvent(
-        "start",
-        { openDownloadsListOnStart: download.openDownloadsListOnStart },
-        download
-      );
+      const announce = () =>
+        this._notifyDownloadEvent(
+          "start",
+          { openDownloadsListOnStart: download.openDownloadsListOnStart },
+          download
+        );
+      // Sval: a peek or tab a link from another app opened, whose first load
+      // became this download, closes before it is announced.
+      const handedOver = lazy.SvalLinkDownloads.handOver(download);
+      if (handedOver) {
+        handedOver.catch(console.error).then(announce);
+      } else {
+        announce();
+      }
     }
   },
 
